# Provenance, not suppression.
#
# examples/cai-delivery.*.json are EMITTED by tools/resign-sample, not authored by hand: it mints a keypair,
# re-signs the sample package with it, and writes the sample, the public key set it verifies against, and
# (historically) the private seed. Declaring that provenance keeps secret scanners from reading a published
# Ed25519 PUBLIC key as a leaked credential, and marks the files as machine output in diffs and language stats.
#
# Nothing here is or ever was a live credential: production does not trust key id `cai-ed25519-sample`, the seed
# it names appears nowhere else in this repository or its deploys, and the tool now writes the private half
# outside the tree entirely. See examples/README.md.
examples/cai-delivery.keys.json linguist-generated=true
examples/cai-delivery.sample.json linguist-generated=true
examples/cai-delivery.sample-key.json linguist-generated=true
